 routines with ParPar’s processing backend, improving par2cmdline’s
 performance on x86/ARM platforms.
 .
 Par2cmdline-turbo aims to keep close with its upstream and mostly differs in
 the following areas related to performance:
  * GF16, MD5 and CRC32 computation, using ParPar’s implementation;
  * ParPar’s internal checksumming to detect RAM errors during GF16
    computation;
  * ParPar’s stitched hashing approach;
  * C++11 threads in place of par2cmdline's OpenMP dependency.
 .
